A. Commit message:
io_uring: check if iowq is killed before queuing

B. Change summary:
This patch ensures that `io_queue_iowq` checks if the task work queue (`io_wq`) has been killed or if the current task is a kernel thread before attempting to queue the request. If either condition is true, it cancels the request with `-ECANCELED`. This prevents potential use-after-free issues when the task work runs after io_uring termination.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/io_uring/io_uring.c b/io_uring/io_uring.c
index 432b95ca9c85e..d3403c8216db8 100644
--- a/io_uring/io_uring.c
+++ b/io_uring/io_uring.c
@@ -514,7 +514,11 @@ static void io_queue_iowq(struct io_kiocb *req)
 	struct io_uring_task *tctx = req->task->io_uring;
 
 	BUG_ON(!tctx);
-	BUG_ON(!tctx->io_wq);
+
+	if ((current->flags & PF_KTHREAD) || !tctx->io_wq) {
+		io_req_task_queue_fail(req, -ECANCELED);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	/* init ->work of the whole link before punting */
 	io_prep_async_link(req);
```